+/// Answers a trapped CPUID with WHP's own default result, with the minimum
+/// set of bits changed that the guest needs to see.
+///
+/// Only the leaves listed in `WHvPartitionPropertyCodeCpuidExitList` reach
+/// here; every other leaf is answered by WHP without an exit. The default
+/// result is preserved wherever it is not explicitly overridden, so that
+/// WHP's feature filtering — which reflects what the partition can actually
+/// execute — is never widened.
+///
+/// Returns the `(eax, ebx, ecx, edx)` to complete the instruction with.
+///
+/// # Leaf 0: maximum standard leaf
+///
+/// EAX is raised to at least 0x15 so that the synthetic TSC leaf installed in
+/// `WhpVm::configure_partition` is reachable. Linux's `native_calibrate_tsc()`
+/// reads leaf 0x15 only when `boot_cpu_data.cpuid_level >= 0x15`; leaf 0 is
+/// otherwise passed through from the host, and AMD hosts stop at 0xD, so on
+/// those hosts the synthesized leaf is written but never read. The vendor
+/// string in EBX/ECX/EDX is left exactly as WHP reported it.
+///
+/// # Leaf 1: feature bits
+///
+/// **ECX bit 21 (x2APIC)** is cleared. The partition is created with
+/// `WHvX64LocalApicEmulationModeXApic`, so there is no x2APIC behind the
+/// advertisement; a guest that believed the bit would drive the APIC through
+/// MSRs the emulated xAPIC does not implement.
+///
+/// **ECX bit 31 (hypervisor present) is deliberately left as WHP set it.**
+/// Setting it is tempting — it is `X86_FEATURE_HYPERVISOR`, and
+/// `ms_hyperv_platform()` returns 0 without it, so it is what would make the
+/// Hyper-V leaves in `WhpVm::configure_partition` reachable. But making them
+/// reachable is not currently an improvement. `ms_hyperv_init_platform()`
+/// (arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mshyperv.c) ends with
+///
+/// ```text
+/// if (!(ms_hyperv.features & HV_ACCESS_TSC_INVARIANT))
+///         mark_tsc_unstable("running on Hyper-V");
+/// ```
+///
+/// and an unstable sched_clock is exactly what engages the
+/// `sched_clock_local()` clamp that froze every printk timestamp in the first
+/// place. Turning this bit on without the rest of the enlightenment story
+/// being true would trade one frozen-clock mechanism for another. The feature
+/// leaf now advertises `HV_ACCESS_TSC_INVARIANT` for that reason, but flipping
+/// this bit remains a separate, deliberate experiment rather than something
+/// bundled into an unrelated fix — not least because doing both at once would
+/// make the next boot's result impossible to attribute.
+///
+/// Everything else in leaf 1, including the APIC ID and topology fields in
+/// EBX, is passed through. Rewriting those is a change to AP bring-up rather
+/// than to timekeeping, and is left alone deliberately.
+#[cfg(target_arch = "x86_64")]
+fn normalize_cpuid(info: &CpuidExitInfo) -> (u64, u64, u64, u64) {
+    /// CPUID leaf 1, ECX bit 21 — x2APIC support.
+    const CPUID_1_ECX_X2APIC: u32 = 1 << 21;
+    /// The lowest maximum-standard-leaf that leaves 0x15 reachable.
+    const MIN_MAX_STANDARD_LEAF: u32 = 0x15;
+
+    let (mut eax, ebx, mut ecx, edx) = (
+        info.default_eax,
+        info.default_ebx,
+        info.default_ecx,
+        info.default_edx,
+    );
+
+    match info.leaf as u32 {
+        0x0 => {
+            eax = u64::from((eax as u32).max(MIN_MAX_STANDARD_LEAF));
+        }
+        0x1 => {
+            ecx = u64::from(ecx as u32 & !CPUID_1_ECX_X2APIC);
+        }
+        // Trapped without a rewrite. Reachable only if the exit list and this
+        // function disagree; replaying the default keeps that a no-op rather
+        // than a hang.
+        _ => {}
+    }
+
+    (eax, ebx, ecx, edx)
+}
+
 /// Encapsulates configuration parameters for the guest vCPUS.
